WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.960
- No, but have you ever
met any of the cast

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:02.860
before doing the movie?

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.890
- I used to work at the Four Seasons Hotel

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.519
in Beverly Hills so I used to
wait on some of these guys.

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:08.380
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.213
- [Sebastian] As a waiter

00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:10.046
I used to --
- [Kelly] Both waiters!

00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:10.879
Get it, get it!
- [Sebastian] Yeah, hello.

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:11.712
Love the waiters.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:13.470
- Seven and a half years.
- Tip them!

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.526
They hate their lives, secretly.

00:00:15.526 --> 00:00:17.420
(laughing loudly)

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.210
- But you waited on who?

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.951
- I waited on anywhere
from Nicole Kidman--

00:00:21.951 --> 00:00:23.001
- Wow.

00:00:23.001 --> 00:00:25.170
- to Al Pacino to Robert De Niro

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.506
and fast forward now 2019, 20,

00:00:28.506 --> 00:00:30.330
I'm in a movie with these guys.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.520
So, I worked there, yeah.
- That's so cool!

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.040
(people clapping)
- Yeah, it's crazy.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.340
- I love you telling that story

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.550
because I think a lot of people out there

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.377
start to give up. They start
to give up and they go,

00:00:39.377 --> 00:00:41.017
"Whatever, okay, I'll
lean into something else.

00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:42.080
"My backup plan or something."

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.510
And that's a really incredible story,

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.570
that's really inspiring.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.450
- Yeah, well I had no backup plan.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.463
- I didn't either.

00:00:47.463 --> 00:00:48.296
(laughing loudly)
- Yeah.

00:00:48.296 --> 00:00:49.526
It was either this or

00:00:49.526 --> 00:00:50.507
the streets.
- [Kelly] Just sink.

00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:51.340
(laughing loudly)

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.465
- So, yeah.

00:00:52.465 --> 00:00:53.940
When I came out to LA in 1998,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.240
it was stand-up comedy or bus.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.490
So yeah, I worked there
seven and half years

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.725
waited on all of Hollywood, and--

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:00.720
- [Kelly] That's so cool.
- Now things

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.070
are finally paying off, so yeah.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.950
- I bet you all of them were
waiters at some point, too.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.040
I feel like we all were waiters.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:05.980
Were you a good waiter?

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:07.190
- I was not only a waiter,

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.509
I was selling satellite dishes--

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:12.630
(laughing loudly)

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.970
out of a kiosk in the ghetto.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:15.880
So--

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.060
- I sold vacuum cleaners for 2 days.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.243
- Is that right?
- Uh huh, and I was like

00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:20.076
"I'm out."
- Door to door?

00:01:20.076 --> 00:01:20.909
- Mm hmm.

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:21.742
- Yeah.

00:01:21.742 --> 00:01:24.058
- The dirt and it was
like, "You know what? "No."

00:01:24.058 --> 00:01:24.891
I couldn't do it.
- Yeah.

00:01:24.891 --> 00:01:27.640
We all had these jobs I used to glaze ham

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.020
at Honey Baked Ham.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.090
- Oh my gosh, those are good!

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.060
(people cheering)

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.640
- Honey Baked Ham, look.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.332
- Those are good!

00:01:34.332 --> 00:01:36.315
I'm serious.
- This one is like, "Yeah!

00:01:36.315 --> 00:01:37.148
"Ham!"

00:01:37.148 --> 00:01:37.981
(laughing loudly)

00:01:37.981 --> 00:01:40.880
- No, we get those for
Christmas and Thanksgiving.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.510
I'm not kidding, they're so good.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.343
- Yeah, I glazed them.

00:01:43.343 --> 00:01:44.580
- Nicely done.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.413
- Yeah.

00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:46.246
- You are great at glazing.
- Thank you.

00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:48.513
- See, it's all this that
builds to where you are now.

